---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Contact Career Portfolio Load Test 01 20260522-042729105';
---

<Layout title={pageTitle}>
  <section class="section-container mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8">
    <header>
      <p class="text-accent">Pages</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-heading font-bold text-maintext">Contact Career Portfolio Load Test 01 20260522-042729105</h1>
      <p class="text-gray">A simple contact page for readers, collaborators, and visitors who need to reach the site.</p>
    </header>
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-maintext">Available contact routes</h2>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">Use [CONTACT_EMAIL] for general enquiries, editorial notes, and messages that do not need a public reply.</p>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">If a newsletter is added later, it should be kept separate from general contact requests.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-maintext">What you can send here</h2>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">Use the published email route for general enquiries, corrections, or messages that do not need a formal support queue.</p>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">The contact page is best suited to questions about project opportunities, speaking requests, collaborations, and professional outreach.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-maintext">What readers should expect</h2>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">Responses, when they are provided, will depend on the type of enquiry and the availability of the editorial team.</p>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">No guaranteed response window is implied unless the site later publishes one as part of a real support or business workflow.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-maintext">How messages are handled</h2>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">Contact messages should be treated as operational communication rather than as public content.</p>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">If more formal handling is required later, the site can add a specific retention or routing policy without changing the basic page structure.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-maintext">Reader corrections and editorial contact</h2>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">For publishing sites, this page also acts as the usual place for corrections, tip-offs, partnership enquiries, and requests related to published material.</p>
        <p class="text-gray leading-relaxed">If contact routes change later, this page should be updated before the old route is removed from the site.</p>
      </section>
  </section>
</Layout>
